{"alignments": [{"id": "HOS.8.3.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.3.001"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.3.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "HOS.8.3.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.3.002"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.3.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "HOS.8.3.a003", "note": "The anarthrous substantive carries the supplied relative frame and copula.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.3.003"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.3.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006", "t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "HOS.8.3.a004", "note": "The anarthrous participle is rendered substantivally.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.3.004"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.3.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "HOS.8.3.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.3.005"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.3.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "HOS.8.3.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.3.006"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.3.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}], "ref": "HOS.8.3", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "HOS.8.4.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.001"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a002", "note": "The causative verb is rendered by the light-verb phrase “have set up kings”; “kings” carries the lexical result and is the target head under rule 44.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.002"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a003", "note": "The waw is rendered by the adversative connective “but.”", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.003"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.004"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a005", "note": "The preposition is rendered as the agentive “by” in “by me.”", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.005"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.006"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a007", "note": "Aligned to the ASV reading “they have made princes,” with “princes” as the lexical result and target head. The noted competing rendering is “they have removed them.”", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.007"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011", "t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.008"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a009", "note": "The subject pronoun realizes the finite verb's person and number.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.010"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015", "t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a010", "note": "The English object pronoun “it” has no corresponding source object morpheme.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.009"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a012", "note": "The material relation expressed by “of” is licensed by the adverbial use of “silver” and remains with that noun.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.011"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019", "t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.012"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a014", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.013"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.015"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a016", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.014"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a017", "note": "The discontinuous English order “have they made” realizes the finite verb, including its subject pronoun.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.016"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t025", "t026", "t027"], "target_head": "t027"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a018", "note": "The dative preposition has no separate English realization in the recasting “made them idols.”", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.017"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.017", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a019", "note": "The suffix is realized by the pronoun “them” after the dative preposition itself is left unrepresented.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.018"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t028"], "target_head": "t028"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a020", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.019"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t029"], "target_head": "t029"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a021", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.020"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t030"], "target_head": "t030"}, {"id": "HOS.8.4.a022", "note": "The supplied subject pronoun and auxiliary sequence belong to the finite passive verb; “cut” is the lexical head and “off” its phrasal particle.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.4.021"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.4.021", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t031", "t032", "t033", "t034", "t035"], "target_head": "t034"}], "ref": "HOS.8.4", "review_notes": ["The alignment follows the ASV's contextual rendering of s007 as “they have made princes”; the briefing records “they have removed them” as the alternative rendering."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "HOS.8.5.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.001"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002", "t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.002"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.003"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a004", "note": "The vocative noun carries the supplied O.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.004"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a005", "note": "The Hebrew verb is rendered by the passive is kindled.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.005"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.006"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.007"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.008"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.009"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a010", "note": "I treated עד מתי and the ASV frame how long will it be as one indivisible interrogative expression; splitting how and long between the particles would be arbitrary.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.010", "WLC.HOS.8.5.011"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.010", "status": "noncompositional", "target": ["t015", "t016", "t017", "t018", "t019"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a011", "note": "The negative force is recast temporally as ere.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.012"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.013"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021", "t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "HOS.8.5.a013", "note": "The supplied function word to belongs to the nominal complement.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.5.014"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.5.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023", "t024"], "target_head": "t024"}], "ref": "HOS.8.5", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "HOS.8.6.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.001"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a002", "note": "The prepositional predicate carries the construction-supplied copula.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.002"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t004"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.003"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a004", "note": "The waw is rendered postpositively by “even.”", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.004"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.005"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a006", "note": "The supplied definite article belongs to the anarthrous noun.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.006"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.007"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.008"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.009"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.010"], "source_head": "WLC.HOS.8.6.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "HOS.8.6.a011", "note": "The predicate noun carries the construction-supplied copula.", "source": ["WLC.HOS.8.6.011"], "source_head": "W